{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 65, :comments ["<b>You will cover</b> — Some say the dagesh in the nun is added, and it is from the root of מִגֵּן צָרֶיךָ (Genesis 14:20), on the pattern of אכילה. But the correct view in my eyes is that it is from גֵּנוּתֵךְ וְהַצֵּל (Isaiah 31:5)." "<b>Your curse</b> — From the root אלה, and the tav is added, like תַּאֲנָתָה מִי יְשִׁיבֶנָּה (Jeremiah 2:24)."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites two comparison verses to argue the root; the second (Isaiah 31:5) contains גנון/והציל, supporting his derivation from גנן rather than גנן with added nun."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:00.595784718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}